{
  "$schema": "../schema/registry.schema.json",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "notes": "Who trained a model, separate from who serves it. A provider id names an inference route (an API account, a gateway, a local runtime); a developer id names the organisation that released the weights or the proprietary model. providerDeveloper maps a first-party provider to the developer it serves so a curated record on that provider inherits it; a host that serves other developers' models (groq, open_router, cheaperinference, nvidia_nim, vercel_gateway) has no entry and every model on it must resolve through an explicit developer field or the author segment of its upstream model id. aliases are matched case-insensitively against that segment; a leading ~ (OpenRouter's latest alias marker) is stripped first.",
